1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,200
This is Shanghai today where the Huangpu curves past the Bund into Pudong.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Along the western mudflats of the Huangpu, international merchants laid the first stone quays of the Bund.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:22,500
Granite banks, the Customs clock tower, and the art-deco crown of the Peace Hotel transformed Shanghai into Paris of the East.

4
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:32,800
For fifty years, while the western shore hummed with density, the eastern peninsula of Pudong remained quiet farmland.

5
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:44,000
In 1990, China designated Pudong a Special Economic Zone. Four years later, the Oriental Pearl Tower sparked a vertical renaissance.

6
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:53,000
Rising eighty-eight storeys, Jin Mao Tower joined traditional Chinese pagoda symmetry with steel and glass.

7
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:63,500
The World Financial Center carved a portal into the clouds, before Shanghai Tower topped out at 632 metres.

8
00:00:64,000 --> 00:00:72,000
Across two centuries of water and ambition, Shanghai built the highest density of human ingenuity on earth.

9
00:00:72,500 --> 00:00:80,500
In thirty years, Pudong transformed from farmland into the world's most dramatic vertical skyline.
